# Codex CLI home is almost entirely app-owned runtime state — auth.json (OAuth
# tokens), a dozen sqlite DBs, sessions/, plus a config.toml that Codex rewrites
# constantly (marketplace revisions, [projects.*] trust levels, [hooks.state]
# trust hashes). ONLY the hand-authored profile overlay is managed; see
# dot_codex/main.config.toml.tmpl for why, and CLAUDE.md "Agent config".
#
# Leaving config.toml unmanaged is also the work/personal boundary: it's where
# carepilot marketplaces and project-trust paths live, and it never reaches the
# public origin because chezmoi doesn't track it.
#
# The bare-directory negation is required — an ignored parent otherwise blocks
# `chezmoi add` of anything beneath it (same reason as the yazi block below).
.codex/**
!.codex
!.codex/main.config.toml

